but the postal music, you know, in the Middle Ages, maḥloqet, open the Shuharu, opinions,

cue0146217
00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:36.220
one says this, the other says that.

cue0146218
00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:42.580
Now, let me ask you from a philosophical point of view, yes?

cue0146219
00:00:43.340 --> 00:00:45.020
Slecha, can anybody close the door, please?

cue0146220
00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:47.800
Because there is a draft, all right?

cue0146221
00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:51.280
Suppose, I don't know

cue0146222
00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:53.280
There is a pasuq

cue0146223
00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:53.940
Alright

cue0146224
00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:57.700
Whatever it is

cue0146225
00:00:57.700 --> 00:00:58.720
So

cue0146226
00:00:58.720 --> 00:01:01.340
I give an expression

cue0146227
00:01:01.340 --> 00:01:01.760
A

cue0146228
00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:05.540
And you give

cue0146229
00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:07.280
An expression

cue0146230
00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:07.780
B

cue0146231
00:01:07.780 --> 00:01:11.140
How can we resolve

cue0146232
00:01:11.140 --> 00:01:12.180
How could

cue0146233
00:01:12.180 --> 00:01:15.420
What we're going to use to resolve this maḥloqet

cue0146234
00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:17.100
In other words, what criteria

cue0146235
00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:24.380
we're going to use. That's my question. Now suppose I want to say, all right, I'm going to use criteria X.

cue0146236
00:01:25.420 --> 00:01:32.620
Listen to this. Is this X written in the Tora? If it's written in the Tora, then let's go to X.

cue0146237
00:01:32.620 --> 00:01:37.820
How could it be a controversy? You understand? How? You're going to say, well no, I'm going to solve it

cue0146238
00:01:37.820 --> 00:01:44.300
through logic. Right? I'm going to solve it through logic. Yes? I'm going to argue my point through logic,

cue0146239
00:01:44.300 --> 00:01:51.300
you are going to appoint through logic. So then it means that the Tora ultimately is conditioned by human logic.

cue0146240
00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:55.300
So how could it be? Something that comes from God is conditioned by human logic.

cue0146241
00:01:55.300 --> 00:02:02.300
The truth is, that's a very important principle of the Geonim and of Rambam, etc.

cue0146242
00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:05.300
So Rabbi David Nieto here, that's going to say this.

cue0146243
00:02:05.300 --> 00:02:10.300
There can never be a maḥloqet on something which is in the Tora.

cue0146244
00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:19.300
There is no mahlukah. There is no controversy. Because if there would be a controversy, there would be no possible way to resolve it.

cue0146245
00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:25.300
The controversies, that's what the point of Rambam makes it very strongly, the Ge'onim and so on.

cue0146246
00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:32.300
The controversies are always undetailed, which are not explicit in the Tora.

cue0146247
00:02:32.300 --> 00:02:37.300
And because they are not explicit in the Tora, then I could say it should be this way.

cue0146248
00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:39.040
Let me give you an example.

cue0146249
00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:42.200
Sefaradim ʾAshkenaz.

cue0146250
00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:46.700
How we put on the tefillin of the hand?

cue0146251
00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:50.720
According to the ʾAshkenaz, you have to stand up.

cue0146252
00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:54.960
According to the Sefaradim, you sit down.

cue0146253
00:02:55.740 --> 00:02:59.520
Now, if you look into the Gemaraʾ, into the whole Gemaraʾ,

cue0146254
00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:02.920
you're not going to find that says,

cue0146255
00:03:03.140 --> 00:03:04.600
tefillin shelyad, you must sit down.

cue0146256
00:03:04.600 --> 00:03:07.180
because if they would say

cue0146257
00:03:07.180 --> 00:03:09.460
then how could ʾAshkenaz stand up

cue0146258
00:03:09.460 --> 00:03:11.440
conversely

cue0146259
00:03:11.440 --> 00:03:13.480
in no place you are going to find a Gemaraʾ

cue0146260
00:03:13.480 --> 00:03:15.620
that says Tefillin Shaliyat

cue0146261
00:03:15.620 --> 00:03:17.820
you have to stand up

cue0146262
00:03:17.820 --> 00:03:18.840
because if we do this

cue0146263
00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:20.140
we are going to say this

cue0146264
00:03:20.140 --> 00:03:23.020
therefore this is

cue0146265
00:03:23.020 --> 00:03:25.400
a question of alright since you are going to

cue0146266
00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:27.100
have two Tefillin more, Tefillin Shaliyat

cue0146267
00:03:27.100 --> 00:03:28.480
Tefillin Sherosh, how you

cue0146268
00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:31.060
you do it, alright

cue0146269
00:03:31.060 --> 00:03:33.220
so one says my opinion is A

cue0146270
00:03:33.220 --> 00:03:34.880
the other says their opinion is B.

cue0146271
00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:35.660
Now,

cue0146272
00:03:36.040 --> 00:03:37.340
that's a very important thing.

cue0146273
00:03:37.600 --> 00:03:38.900
People do not know this.

cue0146274
00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:41.200
If this mahlukah is only on something

cue0146275
00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:42.040
on a detail,

cue0146276
00:03:42.580 --> 00:03:43.600
which is not in the Tora,

cue0146277
00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:45.680
it means the following.

cue0146278
00:03:46.220 --> 00:03:47.360
That if I put it,

cue0146279
00:03:47.420 --> 00:03:48.340
instead of sitting down,

cue0146280
00:03:48.480 --> 00:03:49.140
standing up,

cue0146281
00:03:51.320 --> 00:03:52.480
or instead of standing up,

cue0146282
00:03:52.540 --> 00:03:53.080
I sit down.

cue0146283
00:03:54.440 --> 00:03:55.260
It's alright.

cue0146284
00:03:56.160 --> 00:03:58.580
Because there never could be a controversy,

cue0146285
00:03:58.960 --> 00:04:00.740
that's the point that is very, very important,

cue0146286
00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:02.020
there never was,

cue0146287
00:04:02.020 --> 00:04:03.460
