00:11:57.280 --> 00:12:06.080
In the case of us, Barukh Hashem, we have modern medicine, etc. and you know, like this. But I just wanted to, so this is a statement, May Barava.

cue0146437
00:12:06.080 --> 00:12:16.080
Yes? And it brings no proof, it just says it, and it's accepted by everybody. Again, an example of a tradition from the time of the Emoraim that comes to them,

cue0146438
00:12:16.080 --> 00:12:18.840
Not via the Mishna or the beraitaʾ.

cue0146439
00:12:19.560 --> 00:12:20.060
The Marava.

cue0146440
00:12:20.840 --> 00:12:23.680
In de tarte one, de serihan le adade,

cue0146441
00:12:24.940 --> 00:12:27.140
shilo ke sidran, terefa.

cue0146442
00:12:27.900 --> 00:12:28.240
All right?

cue0146443
00:12:29.180 --> 00:12:35.160
Now, the lung has partitions.

cue0146444
00:12:35.780 --> 00:12:35.960
Yes?

cue0146445
00:12:36.460 --> 00:12:36.760
All right?

cue0146446
00:12:37.500 --> 00:12:38.780
You know, partitions.

cue0146447
00:12:38.960 --> 00:12:39.880
It's not one thing.

cue0146448
00:12:39.880 --> 00:12:41.620
It's made up actually of five things.

cue0146449
00:12:42.100 --> 00:12:44.440
And the things are called Onot.

cue0146450
00:12:44.440 --> 00:12:46.960
Each one of those compartments

cue0146451
00:12:46.960 --> 00:12:48.460
If they are tied

cue0146452
00:12:48.460 --> 00:12:50.740
One with the other

cue0146453
00:12:50.740 --> 00:12:52.580
Sheloke Sidran

cue0146454
00:12:52.580 --> 00:12:54.180
Not in the proper order

cue0146455
00:12:54.180 --> 00:12:56.740
The one that is supposed to be on top is on the bottom

cue0146456
00:12:56.740 --> 00:12:58.780
And the one at the bottom is on the top

cue0146457
00:12:58.780 --> 00:12:59.900
Yes

cue0146458
00:12:59.900 --> 00:13:01.840
The animal is tied

cue0146459
00:13:01.840 --> 00:13:03.060
Although it has all the

cue0146460
00:13:03.060 --> 00:13:04.960
The lungs

cue0146461
00:13:04.960 --> 00:13:06.680
But it's not

cue0146462
00:13:06.680 --> 00:13:07.820
Sheloke Sidran

cue0146463
00:13:07.820 --> 00:13:09.460
It's no good

cue0146464
00:13:09.460 --> 00:13:13.960
Do you understand what I'm saying?

cue0146465
00:13:14.440 --> 00:13:15.480
What is the word?

cue0146466
00:13:16.160 --> 00:13:19.000
Ona is the thing that fills with air.

cue0146467
00:13:19.380 --> 00:13:25.240
It means there's five compartments in the lung, yes, of the animal or our things.

cue0146468
00:13:25.480 --> 00:13:26.700
The five things, yes.

cue0146469
00:13:27.180 --> 00:13:29.360
And there's the upper part.

cue0146470
00:13:30.180 --> 00:13:31.140
It's lobes.

cue0146471
00:13:31.520 --> 00:13:32.380
It's called lobes?

cue0146472
00:13:32.500 --> 00:13:32.940
Lobes.

cue0146473
00:13:33.040 --> 00:13:35.240
Two on the left, three on the right.

cue0146474
00:13:35.360 --> 00:13:35.480
Yes.

cue0146475
00:13:35.840 --> 00:13:38.420
Now, the ona is called in English lobes.

cue0146476
00:13:38.800 --> 00:13:43.020
If the lobes are not in the order, the one that's supposed to be down is up,

cue0146477
00:13:43.020 --> 00:13:44.100
or up is down.

cue0146478
00:13:44.440 --> 00:13:47.040
the animal is a defect.

cue0146479
00:13:47.720 --> 00:13:47.920
Alright?

cue0146480
00:13:48.480 --> 00:13:51.180
It's a defect. A generic defect.

cue0146481
00:13:51.960 --> 00:14:02.500
The law is the following.

cue0146482
00:14:03.140 --> 00:14:04.020
In the Re'ah,

cue0146483
00:14:05.000 --> 00:14:06.180
there are two skins.

cue0146484
00:14:07.260 --> 00:14:08.240
It has two skins.

cue0146485
00:14:08.240 --> 00:14:09.040
Right?

cue0146486
00:14:09.900 --> 00:14:11.940
If only one skin

cue0146487
00:14:11.940 --> 00:14:14.000
has a hole,

cue0146488
00:14:14.440 --> 00:14:27.440
whether the upper one or the lower one, it's not Taref. It's only Taref when they have a Nekeb, a hole that goes through both skins.

cue0146489
00:14:27.440 --> 00:14:42.440
Now, this is law number one, I want you to understand. So if they have, if the Nekeb pierce through both skins, then and then alone is Taref.

cue0146490
00:14:42.440 --> 00:14:54.440
Sometimes the animal has a hole in the rea and then a buaa grows on top of it.

cue0146491
00:14:54.440 --> 00:14:59.440
A buaa is like a skin, a very thin skin.

cue0146492
00:14:59.440 --> 00:15:01.440
Like a cyst.

cue0146493
00:15:01.440 --> 00:15:02.440
Like a cyst.

cue0146494
00:15:02.440 --> 00:15:05.440
Just like in your, for instance, if you get burned.

cue0146495
00:15:05.440 --> 00:15:07.440
If you get burned.

cue0146496
00:15:07.440 --> 00:15:09.440
Like a scar.

cue0146497
00:15:09.440 --> 00:15:14.380
scar. Like a, you know, like a, like sometimes you get burned or you get, and you could be

cue0146498
00:15:14.380 --> 00:15:19.600
something like white in your, in your skin, be full of water, you know. Not a blister,

cue0146499
00:15:19.840 --> 00:15:25.600
a blister, a blister, like full of water, you know. So this is called, that is a bu'a.

cue0146500
00:15:25.760 --> 00:15:31.920
Listen to this. Now, you have, now you, you're a shahid, you open and you look into the re'a,

cue0146501
00:15:31.920 --> 00:15:43.100
you look into the lungs, and you see if there is a bu'am, one single bu'am, yes, then you could be bodek,

cue0146502
00:15:44.020 --> 00:15:45.560
and find out the following.

cue0146503
00:15:45.740 --> 00:15:54.020
So a good bodek could tell you whether this is covering a hole, in which case the animal is taref,

cue0146504
00:15:54.100 --> 00:15:55.560
in your opinion, not permitted to eat it.

cue0146505
00:15:55.560 --> 00:15:58.620
Or sometimes it grows like this.

cue0146506
00:15:59.060 --> 00:16:00.820
It grows like that.

cue0146507
00:16:01.500 --> 00:16:02.140
Without a hole.

cue0146508
00:16:02.840 --> 00:16:04.620
So now, you have the Re'ah.

cue0146509
00:16:04.840 --> 00:16:05.560
And you have the Shohayt.

cue0146510
00:16:06.460 --> 00:16:08.360
And there is a Bu'ah.

cue0146511
00:16:09.400 --> 00:16:12.620
Bu'ah means one single thing like this.

cue0146512
00:16:13.420 --> 00:16:16.760
So, if it's one alone,

cue0146513
00:16:18.440 --> 00:16:19.640
then you could bodek.

cue0146514
00:16:19.780 --> 00:16:20.380
You make Bedika.

cue0146515
00:16:20.520 --> 00:16:21.700
I'll tell you in a second how you make Bedika.

cue0146516
00:16:22.680 --> 00:16:23.860
You make Bedika.

cue0146517
00:16:23.860 --> 00:16:27.560
and you see whether actually there is a hole,

cue0146518
00:16:30.460 --> 00:16:32.080
in which case is taref,

cue0146519
00:16:33.000 --> 00:16:34.440
or there is no hole,

cue0146520
00:16:35.500 --> 00:16:36.680
in that case,

cue0146521
00:16:37.460 --> 00:16:37.920
is kasher.

cue0146522
00:16:38.620 --> 00:16:39.480
How do you make medica?

cue0146523
00:16:39.640 --> 00:16:40.020
Very simple.

cue0146524
00:16:40.620 --> 00:16:41.100
You take,

cue0146525
00:16:42.040 --> 00:16:43.820
that's the way Rambam says it,

cue0146526
00:16:43.900 --> 00:16:46.120
that's the way the Temanim say,

cue0146527
00:16:46.200 --> 00:16:46.980
we don't do it this way.

cue0146528
00:16:47.280 --> 00:16:50.380
But just let me tell you first the way the Rambam and the Temanim,

cue0146529
00:16:50.460 --> 00:16:50.860
they do it,

cue0146530
00:16:51.060 --> 00:16:51.940
which I think is the best.

cue0146531
00:16:52.340 --> 00:16:53.320
But we don't do it this way.

cue0146532
00:16:53.320 --> 00:17:00.520
They take a lukewarm water, you put the Re'a there, and then you blow it.

cue0146533
00:17:01.580 --> 00:17:06.720
If there's bubbles coming out, that means that there's a hole.

cue0146534
00:17:08.280 --> 00:17:08.580
You see?

cue0146535
00:17:09.400 --> 00:17:13.240
If there are no bubbles coming out, then there is Kisera.

cue0146536
00:17:13.760 --> 00:17:15.720
That's the way Rambam says to make Vedika.

cue0146537
00:17:16.220 --> 00:17:17.120
We make it, what?

cue0146538
00:17:17.400 --> 00:17:19.140
It is a hole, and it's covering it up.

cue0146539
00:17:19.340 --> 00:17:19.520
How is it?

cue0146540
00:17:20.340 --> 00:17:22.440
Oh, it will come out through, I'm sorry,

cue0146541
00:17:22.440 --> 00:17:23.200
then you would see,

cue0146542
00:17:23.420 --> 00:17:25.820
then you would see this bu'ah standing up.

cue0146543
00:17:26.480 --> 00:17:27.440
Because the...

cue0146544
00:17:29.280 --> 00:17:30.400
It looks like a bubble.

cue0146545
00:17:30.780 --> 00:17:30.900
Yes.

cue0146546
00:17:31.100 --> 00:17:31.420
And also,

cue0146547
00:17:31.480 --> 00:17:33.580
bubble will come out from the skin.

cue0146548
00:17:34.240 --> 00:17:34.620
Will not,

cue0146549
00:17:34.700 --> 00:17:35.080
will not,

cue0146550
00:17:35.320 --> 00:17:36.380
the skin apparently,

cue0146551
00:17:36.860 --> 00:17:37.580
I'm not,

cue0146552
00:17:37.820 --> 00:17:40.360
it does not close things hermetically.

cue0146553
00:17:40.840 --> 00:17:40.960
Alright.

cue0146554
00:17:41.620 --> 00:17:42.840
We don't do it this way.

cue0146555
00:17:43.320 --> 00:17:43.960
The Sefaradim,

cue0146556
00:17:44.160 --> 00:17:44.980
also the ʾAshkenaz,

cue0146557
00:17:45.100 --> 00:17:45.980
also don't do it this way.

cue0146558
00:17:46.360 --> 00:17:46.880
How they do it,

cue0146559
00:17:46.900 --> 00:17:47.860
Sefaradim and ʾAshkenaz,

cue0146560
00:17:48.340 --> 00:17:50.600
they do it by blowing it without the hot water.

cue0146561
00:17:50.600 --> 00:17:52.260
Without the lukewarm water.

cue0146562
00:17:52.260 --> 00:18:05.100
Why? Because they're afraid that the lukewarm water maybe is going to, there's some dirt from the animal, you know, blood and so on, and will be so them, they make it.

cue0146563
00:18:05.520 --> 00:18:08.740
You see? No, close it. Close it.

cue0146564
00:18:08.960 --> 00:18:15.260
So therefore, we do it, and I did it, and I saw it many times, although I'm not an expert, I'm not a bodek, yes?

cue0146565
00:18:15.260 --> 00:18:17.800
but I saw it many times and I was taught how to do it.

cue0146566
00:18:18.360 --> 00:18:21.240
We blow it and then somebody else looks into it

cue0146567
00:18:21.240 --> 00:18:23.480
and see whether the thing is standing or not.

cue0146568
00:18:23.700 --> 00:18:27.760
If it's standing, then obviously it has a hole.

cue0146569
00:18:28.100 --> 00:18:30.880
And if it is not standing, that means that there is no hole.

cue0146570
00:18:31.520 --> 00:18:34.600
Or if there is a hole, maybe on one skin, but not on both skins.

cue0146571
00:18:35.280 --> 00:18:35.560
You see?

cue0146572
00:18:36.240 --> 00:18:37.300
And that is kosher.

cue0146573
00:18:37.680 --> 00:18:41.820
However, if there are two bu'at,

cue0146574
00:18:41.820 --> 00:18:45.380
not one bu'ah

cue0146575
00:18:45.380 --> 00:18:48.140
the law is we don't make medica

cue0146576
00:18:48.140 --> 00:18:49.140
we declare tarif

cue0146577
00:18:49.140 --> 00:18:52.320
you see and al-Ambam says

cue0146578
00:18:52.320 --> 00:18:53.960
why he says because maybe the

cue0146579
00:18:53.960 --> 00:18:55.540
hole is in between them

cue0146580
00:18:55.540 --> 00:18:57.060
and then you cannot

cue0146581
00:18:57.060 --> 00:18:59.300
it's not that each one is covering

cue0146582
00:18:59.300 --> 00:19:00.080
a

cue0146583
00:19:00.080 --> 00:19:04.340
a different hole

cue0146584
00:19:04.340 --> 00:19:05.860
but between both of them

cue0146585
00:19:05.860 --> 00:19:08.460
between two of them there is one single hole

cue0146586
00:19:08.460 --> 00:19:10.020
and sometimes it is

cue0146587
00:19:10.020 --> 00:19:14.120
and therefore by blowing it this way you cannot make, it cannot tell.

cue0146588
00:19:14.820 --> 00:19:20.240
Now, no, no, two, one, no, no, one, you know, if they're two, together, together.

cue0146589
00:19:20.580 --> 00:19:23.640
And also, how do you know whether they are called together or they are separate?

cue0146590
00:19:23.900 --> 00:19:24.400
Very simple.

cue0146591
00:19:24.700 --> 00:19:25.700
You blow one of them.

cue0146592
00:19:26.820 --> 00:19:28.740
If the other one stands, it means that they are together.

cue0146593
00:19:30.280 --> 00:19:30.620
You see?

cue0146594
00:19:31.300 --> 00:19:34.600
In this case, we don't care.

cue0146595
00:19:34.760 --> 00:19:37.200
We don't make the pedicab of the two.

cue0146596
00:19:37.200 --> 00:19:42.640
If they are together, this is where the glatt kosher, non-glatt kosher comes about.

cue0146597
00:19:43.240 --> 00:19:46.560
The glatt kosher means that if you see anything in the lung,

cue0146598
00:19:47.680 --> 00:19:51.320
immediately, two bo'od, one bo'ah, you don't make bedikah.

cue0146599
00:19:52.020 --> 00:19:55.700
Immediately you kill it, unkosher, you give it to the unkosher butcher.

cue0146600
00:19:56.320 --> 00:19:59.640
But according to the non-glad, you are bodek.

cue0146601
00:19:59.980 --> 00:20:02.000
And I told you the history of it, it's very simple.

cue0146602
00:20:02.000 --> 00:20:07.260
in ʾAshkenaz communities, they were limited, the amount of animals that they were given

cue0146603
00:20:07.260 --> 00:20:09.740
by the goyim to sort, even in modern times.

cue0146604
00:20:10.240 --> 00:20:14.660
And therefore, they had to, for example, in a village, they give you five cows.

cue0146605
00:20:15.220 --> 00:20:19.980
So if you're going to say that two cows are taref, then two-thirds of the meat product is this.

cue0146606
00:20:20.220 --> 00:20:24.360
So they were much careful, and before they created taref, they would make all kinds of bedikot,

cue0146607
00:20:24.400 --> 00:20:28.780
and we trust, of course, that a shahad is a trustworthy, should be a trustworthy individual,

cue0146608
00:20:29.120 --> 00:20:31.420
and therefore, if he tells you he's kasher, it should be kasher.

cue0146609
00:20:31.420 --> 00:20:33.720
It's not going to be just like that.

cue0146610
00:20:34.000 --> 00:20:34.400
Bernie.

cue0146611
00:20:34.600 --> 00:20:39.220
I was told that in the past, maybe 20 years ago, 30 years ago,

cue0146612
00:20:39.260 --> 00:20:40.940
there was no concept of kosher, black kosher.

cue0146613
00:20:41.120 --> 00:20:42.040
Absolutely correct.

cue0146614
00:20:42.580 --> 00:20:43.460
Absolutely correct.

cue0146615
00:20:43.620 --> 00:20:44.660
Where did it come all of a sudden in?

cue0146616
00:20:44.740 --> 00:20:46.140
I want to tell you how it came.

cue0146617
00:20:47.440 --> 00:20:50.280
It came, incidentally, a teacher of my teacher,

cue0146618
00:20:50.340 --> 00:20:52.320
Bisaak of al-A'afi al-A'afi al-Shalom, was involved in this thing.

cue0146619
00:20:53.020 --> 00:20:57.140
Many years ago, the Turks, they only recognized the Sefaradim.

cue0146620
00:20:57.680 --> 00:20:58.740
They didn't recognize ʾAshkenaz.

cue0146621
00:20:58.740 --> 00:21:03.160
simply because we were citizens of Turkish territory

cue0146622
00:21:03.160 --> 00:21:05.120
and ʾAshkenaz, they were not

cue0146623
00:21:05.120 --> 00:21:09.780
so they were, they wanted to have Shehita

cue0146624
00:21:09.780 --> 00:21:13.200
separate Shehita, the ʾAshkenaz

cue0146625
00:21:13.200 --> 00:21:17.320
in Israel, for economic reasons

cue0146626
00:21:17.320 --> 00:21:20.360
they wanted to sell to the people, listen, it's an income

cue0146627
00:21:20.360 --> 00:21:24.480
they wanted to have the income for them, rather than this

cue0146628
00:21:24.480 --> 00:21:35.480
So the question was, I'm sorry, at one time the Turkish government gave to one ʾAshkenaz group permission to make shahita.

cue0146629
00:21:35.480 --> 00:21:44.480
So then they came the Hasidim or other, I don't know from where or not, and they apparently didn't get along with the other group, and they wanted to open their own shahita.

cue0146630
00:21:44.480 --> 00:21:50.480
So now the Turkish says, well, we are ʾAshkenaz, we are Separatists, what do you want? Another one.

cue0146631
00:21:50.480 --> 00:21:57.460
want. So they say, ah, we are ʾAshkenaz, but we want to make the laws not like this they make

cue0146632
00:21:57.460 --> 00:22:04.900
with the re'ah, we want to make it halak, you know, glad like the Sepher Adim. So, and therefore

cue0146633
00:22:04.900 --> 00:22:10.020
we want to have separate thing. So the teacher of my teacher, Bishak Abu'l-Afil, was one of the

cue0146634
00:22:10.020 --> 00:22:15.260
ones, he was in Tiberias at the time, he intervened on behalf of the ʾAshkenaz to get them, let them

cue0146635
00:22:15.260 --> 00:22:19.460
have a permit from the Turkish government probably because maybe had

cue0146636
00:22:19.460 --> 00:22:24.140
pulled with I don't know exactly the bureaucracy and they were able to get

cue0146637
00:22:24.140 --> 00:22:29.960
the permit so and therefore now they justify the shahita as being

cue0146638
00:22:29.960 --> 00:22:36.420
glad. Now in America when I came to America there was no such a concept of

cue0146639
00:22:36.420 --> 00:22:42.580
glatt kosher. There was none. Why? Because the ʾAshkenaz of the ʾAshkenaz

cue0146640
00:22:42.580 --> 00:22:48.740
they were in charge of sheikhah, they were not from the Hasidim, you see, and they were came from

cue0146641
00:22:48.740 --> 00:22:55.540
Vasha, from Minsk, or Pinsk, or one of the large cities, and those cities they had ration, they rationed

cue0146642
00:22:55.540 --> 00:23:02.420
the cows, and they would make shaitan, not according to, not glad. I ate from it. Why? Because the law is as

cue0146643
00:23:02.420 --> 00:23:08.900
simple as this. Yes, we say, we eat halak. That's the malan, says the tzatzik.

cue0146644
00:23:08.900 --> 00:23:10.420
Not one bu'a?

cue0146645
00:23:10.420 --> 00:23:18.900
Not one bu'a, if there's a bu'a, no, it is bu'a, one bu'a, no, even one bu'a they don't, they don't, they don't, they throw it.

cue0146646
00:23:18.900 --> 00:23:24.900
And I told you the reason why, because we used to be slaughtering the same slaughterhouse as the mas'in, why should we even,

cue0146647
00:23:24.900 --> 00:23:33.300
it's more waste time to be bodek this bu'a than to give it to the goy and you take another one and you shohed.

cue0146648
00:23:33.300 --> 00:23:40.300
was the problem. It's much easier. Alright. So by law, that was the custom. But here comes a point, a very important point.

cue0146649
00:23:40.300 --> 00:23:46.300
There was a question as to the Hidah. Haim David, the Sepher Zulay, I want to get Ḥakhamim.

cue0146650
00:23:46.300 --> 00:23:54.300
He says, you are a Sepher Adi, Shaliyah, from Erez Israel. So the Shaliyah ended up going to travel all over the world.

cue0146651
00:23:54.300 --> 00:24:01.300
Now you are in a place in which the Sheikha Hidah is only ʾAshkenaz. Alright. Non-Glad.

cue0146652
00:24:01.300 --> 00:24:07.280
Yoseph, al-Adi, you follow my lad. Can you eat from that shechitah? He says, of course you can.

