00:36:54.160 --> 00:36:54.780
You make shahita,

cue0146869
00:36:55.480 --> 00:36:57.220
but providing that then you have to make

cue0146870
00:36:57.220 --> 00:36:59.680
a bedika on the animal, because it was

cue0146871
00:36:59.680 --> 00:36:59.960
thrown.

cue0146872
00:37:01.880 --> 00:37:03.380
Sometimes they throw it, of course.

cue0146873
00:37:03.540 --> 00:37:05.600
And they put it on the ground. And they throw it in a way

cue0146874
00:37:05.600 --> 00:37:06.820
that against the spine.

cue0146875
00:37:07.240 --> 00:37:09.380
If you throw it against the spine within a second,

cue0146876
00:37:09.860 --> 00:37:10.160
then

cue0146877
00:37:10.160 --> 00:37:12.860
you make shahita.

cue0146878
00:37:13.200 --> 00:37:15.080
But when you make shahita, you have to be bodeg,

cue0146879
00:37:15.080 --> 00:37:20.280
because it may, you may have broken a vertebrate. Yes, Rod?

cue0146880
00:37:20.280 --> 00:37:25.880
In the first case, if it's the outside that's broken, it would be pretty easy to see.

cue0146881
00:37:25.880 --> 00:37:26.480
That's right.

cue0146882
00:37:26.480 --> 00:37:28.280
But if it's something inside...

cue0146883
00:37:28.280 --> 00:37:30.080
No, but now suppose you see it broken.

cue0146884
00:37:30.080 --> 00:37:32.680
But if it's the outside, then the animal's going to be lame or...

cue0146885
00:37:32.680 --> 00:37:38.280
No, yeah, but it happens this, this normally happens when you're throwing the animal to Shobha,

cue0146886
00:37:38.280 --> 00:37:44.080
because the Jews in my days, now they do it differently, they have a machine and they pull the leg of the animal up.

cue0146887
00:37:44.080 --> 00:37:46.640
In my day, they didn't use it this way.

cue0146888
00:37:46.900 --> 00:37:48.660
They used to literally bring it to the floor.

cue0146889
00:37:49.680 --> 00:37:51.240
Yes, and they used to hold it.

cue0146890
00:37:51.780 --> 00:37:54.400
Two guys to hold the cow,

cue0146891
00:37:54.680 --> 00:37:57.420
and the shahid sits on top of it and makes shaitan.

cue0146892
00:37:57.960 --> 00:37:58.360
All right?

cue0146893
00:37:59.120 --> 00:38:00.380
That's the way they used to do it.

cue0146894
00:38:00.520 --> 00:38:01.820
So when you throw the animal,

cue0146895
00:38:03.000 --> 00:38:06.140
sometimes you break the spine.

cue0146896
00:38:06.860 --> 00:38:07.140
You see?

cue0146897
00:38:07.640 --> 00:38:11.000
So today the animal is held from the legs,

cue0146898
00:38:11.000 --> 00:38:15.480
there's something pulling the animal, you know, up.

cue0146899
00:38:16.340 --> 00:38:18.620
But in my days, there was no machine.

cue0146900
00:38:18.920 --> 00:38:20.980
They just literally brought the animal down,

cue0146901
00:38:22.040 --> 00:38:25.020
they make it lose the hind legs, the balance,

cue0146902
00:38:25.400 --> 00:38:27.560
the animal falls, and they stay on top of it,

cue0146903
00:38:27.820 --> 00:38:29.800
they hold it, the people, they know how to do it.

cue0146904
00:38:30.440 --> 00:38:32.000
Like a wrestling, like a...

cue0146905
00:38:32.000 --> 00:38:32.460
Yes.

cue0146906
00:38:32.960 --> 00:38:33.800
Like a rodeo.

cue0146907
00:38:34.120 --> 00:38:36.580
By the way, many of the animals on the rodeo,

cue0146908
00:38:36.640 --> 00:38:37.320
you could be sure,

cue0146909
00:38:37.600 --> 00:38:39.360
some of them, their spine is broken.

cue0146910
00:38:39.360 --> 00:38:41.680
The way they do it with the lasso, the goyim.

cue0146911
00:38:42.160 --> 00:38:43.120
The spine is broken.

cue0146912
00:38:43.800 --> 00:38:46.540
And so, all right.

cue0146913
00:38:46.820 --> 00:38:49.860
So now, here it is interesting.

cue0146914
00:38:50.800 --> 00:38:51.880
What the Mishna says.

cue0146915
00:38:52.380 --> 00:38:54.220
Raḇ chut ha-shidra.

cue0146916
00:38:55.980 --> 00:38:58.700
Now, you see.

cue0146917
00:38:59.360 --> 00:39:00.080
This is an example.

cue0146918
00:39:00.820 --> 00:39:02.360
Shechorkim al-pilusha ha-ikar.

cue0146919
00:39:02.660 --> 00:39:04.340
All of them, they have the same ha-ikar.

cue0146920
00:39:04.480 --> 00:39:06.580
It has to be the Raḇ chut ha-shidra.

cue0146921
00:39:06.580 --> 00:39:12.340
The maḥloqet is what constitutes Raḇ. The outer Raḇ or the inner Raḇ.

cue0146922
00:39:12.340 --> 00:39:13.340
Alright?

cue0146923
00:39:13.340 --> 00:39:19.620
Not on the Akal itself, but on the Akal, on the law that we receive that has to be Raḇ

cue0146924
00:39:19.620 --> 00:39:20.620
Chuta Shidra.

cue0146925
00:39:20.620 --> 00:39:21.620
And there is no maḥloqet.

cue0146926
00:39:21.620 --> 00:39:26.620
The maḥloqet is what does it mean the word Raḇ Chuta Shidra.

cue0146927
00:39:26.620 --> 00:39:27.620
Alright?

cue0146928
00:39:27.620 --> 00:39:33.620
And what is more important than the Se'et and the Oz, that the Akal are all qabbala

cue0146929
00:39:33.620 --> 00:39:38.940
Moshi Mishinai. And the proof that all these principles, for instance, that they had the principle

cue0146930
00:39:38.940 --> 00:39:46.620
if Raḇ Chut Hashira, the animal is Taleb. They had the principle. What they didn't have, that's the principle

cue0146931
00:39:46.620 --> 00:39:51.740
they had in qabbala and Moshi Mishinai. What they didn't have is what constitutes Raḇ, is it the outer

cue0146932
00:39:51.740 --> 00:39:57.700
circle or the inner circle? That's the controversy. That's the Mahloka, yes. Alright.

cue0146933
00:39:57.700 --> 00:40:00.340
And what is more harmful and more harmful than the Akarim,

cue0146934
00:40:00.380 --> 00:40:02.500
is that the Tanahim at that time

cue0146935
00:40:02.500 --> 00:40:03.680
did not have the law of the Akarim.

cue0146936
00:40:04.320 --> 00:40:05.420
They never the Tanahim,

cue0146937
00:40:05.700 --> 00:40:07.500
there is a law of the Tanahim at this point.

cue0146938
00:40:08.500 --> 00:40:11.820
As we saw in the case of Shofar and Arash,

cue0146939
00:40:12.080 --> 00:40:13.900
there is no law of the Akarim,

cue0146940
00:40:14.180 --> 00:40:16.080
all the law is on the

cue0146941
00:40:16.080 --> 00:40:18.540
interpretations or the applications of the Akarim.

cue0146942
00:40:19.100 --> 00:40:19.200
Alright.

cue0146943
00:40:20.820 --> 00:40:21.260
Now,

cue0146944
00:40:22.480 --> 00:40:23.640
it says,

cue0146945
00:40:25.520 --> 00:40:27.020
I think it's late, no?

cue0146946
00:40:27.700 --> 00:40:47.980
Is it late? I have time. I'm married. I have grandchildren. I don't have to, you know, do this. But if any of you think that it's a little bit late, don't be shy. You're making a Messiah, you tell him, because otherwise you're not going to come next week. So I want you to come. So is it, do I have five, ten more minutes? You sure? All right.

cue0146947
00:40:47.980 --> 00:40:53.720
I remember when I was a younger person

cue0146948
00:40:53.720 --> 00:40:57.660
that I found in the introduction to Al-Ambab

cue0146949
00:40:57.660 --> 00:40:59.120
that we studied last year

cue0146950
00:40:59.120 --> 00:41:09.400
He says that every Rabbi

cue0146951
00:41:09.400 --> 00:41:10.740
prior to Rabbeinu Qadosh

cue0146952
00:41:10.740 --> 00:41:15.260
they would write privately notes

cue0146953
00:41:15.260 --> 00:41:16.940
about the Tora

cue0146954
00:41:16.940 --> 00:41:22.940
The notes were never published, but they were each person, because nobody could remember everything.

cue0146955
00:41:22.940 --> 00:41:27.940
I mean even the greatest memory, you know, you cannot remember everything.

cue0146956
00:41:27.940 --> 00:41:33.940
So it says they used to write private notes. Everybody has a lot of notebooks and used to write the Tora.

cue0146957
00:41:33.940 --> 00:41:35.940
Alright?

cue0146958
00:41:35.940 --> 00:41:39.300
what he heard from his teachers.

cue0146959
00:41:41.680 --> 00:41:44.520
Also, from laws that they were invented.

cue0146960
00:41:44.960 --> 00:41:45.760
In every generation,

cue0146961
00:41:45.920 --> 00:41:47.100
invent new laws.

cue0146962
00:41:51.840 --> 00:41:53.580
This is pertaining to laws

cue0146963
00:41:53.580 --> 00:41:55.580
that they were not learned through tradition.

cue0146964
00:41:59.920 --> 00:42:01.580
Only through exegesis,

cue0146965
00:42:01.780 --> 00:42:02.980
through derasha.

cue0146966
00:42:03.240 --> 00:42:04.880
There are 13 ways of making derasha.

cue0146967
00:42:05.940 --> 00:42:17.520
And the Supreme Court of Israel passed the approval on those laws, so also they wrote down each one in his notes.

cue0146968
00:42:19.500 --> 00:42:22.520
And it always was like this. I'll explain everything, don't worry.

cue0146969
00:42:26.640 --> 00:42:28.600
Now the question that I have is the following.

cue0146970
00:42:29.260 --> 00:42:32.080
If Moses received the Tora with all the explanations,

cue0146971
00:42:32.080 --> 00:42:35.620
and with all the principles

cue0146972
00:42:35.620 --> 00:42:37.780
and all the details

cue0146973
00:42:37.780 --> 00:42:39.480
and all the

cue0146974
00:42:39.480 --> 00:42:41.620
minute, smallest

cue0146975
00:42:41.620 --> 00:42:42.140
details.

cue0146976
00:42:43.440 --> 00:42:45.640
How my mind could write

cue0146977
00:42:45.640 --> 00:42:46.980
that there were things

cue0146978
00:42:46.980 --> 00:42:49.900
there were things

cue0146979
00:42:49.900 --> 00:42:51.900
that were in every generation

cue0146980
00:42:51.900 --> 00:42:53.620
that were

cue0146981
00:42:53.620 --> 00:42:54.800
new

cue0146982
00:42:54.800 --> 00:42:56.480
and also

cue0146983
00:42:56.480 --> 00:42:59.700
why is it necessary

cue0146984
00:42:59.700 --> 00:43:01.380
to have a Hiddush?

cue0146985
00:43:01.380 --> 00:43:10.520
Now, briefly, this is, you see, on the basis of these questions, I learned, I became, my mind became, you know, I learned from these questions, from the Hakan David Nieto.

cue0146986
00:43:11.100 --> 00:43:18.840
And, of course, I had my book, Yorim Bebishe Teran Ramban, which I devote to my, almost, the majority of the book, to answer this question.

cue0146987
00:43:19.640 --> 00:43:20.940
Because they are very important questions.

cue0146988
00:43:21.120 --> 00:43:25.620
I mean, if you have, if everything came out from Moshe Misinai, then how could you have a Hadush?

cue0146989
00:43:26.460 --> 00:43:27.900
Alright, now listen to this.

cue0146990
00:43:28.720 --> 00:43:29.380
Very simple.

cue0146991
00:43:29.380 --> 00:43:32.080
And I, Barukh Hashem, afterwards

cue0146992
00:43:32.080 --> 00:43:33.580
I wrote about it in

cue0146993
00:43:33.580 --> 00:43:35.420
Of course in Hebrew

cue0146994
00:43:35.420 --> 00:43:38.300
And also I wrote about it in English, in several articles

cue0146995
00:43:38.300 --> 00:43:40.320
And also I have, in French

cue0146996
00:43:40.320 --> 00:43:41.680
I have a long, long

cue0146997
00:43:41.680 --> 00:43:44.160
135, 140 pages

cue0146998
00:43:44.160 --> 00:43:46.060
Article in French about this

cue0146999
00:43:46.060 --> 00:43:47.380
This thing, and

cue0147000
00:43:47.380 --> 00:43:49.360
No, no, because I'm, it's very

cue0147001
00:43:49.360 --> 00:43:51.560
Not everybody knows it, you know

cue0147002
00:43:51.560 --> 00:43:54.220
And I develop it in a legal sense

cue0147003
00:43:54.220 --> 00:43:54.680
Anyhow

cue0147004
00:43:54.680 --> 00:43:56.980
Briefly it's like this

cue0147005
00:43:56.980 --> 00:43:58.300
We have a Tora

cue0147006
00:43:58.300 --> 00:44:00.500
and the Tora

cue0147007
00:44:00.500 --> 00:44:02.020
it's explicit

cue0147008
00:44:02.020 --> 00:44:02.580
the one

cue0147009
00:44:02.580 --> 00:44:03.300
told

cue0147010
00:44:03.300 --> 00:44:05.560
he told them

cue0147011
00:44:05.560 --> 00:44:06.220
it has to be

cue0147012
00:44:06.220 --> 00:44:06.580
square

cue0147013
00:44:06.580 --> 00:44:06.980
it has to be

cue0147014
00:44:06.980 --> 00:44:07.320
black

cue0147015
00:44:07.320 --> 00:44:07.820
it has to be

cue0147016
00:44:07.820 --> 00:44:08.560
this

cue0147017
00:44:08.560 --> 00:44:09.600
all the details

cue0147018
00:44:09.600 --> 00:44:10.280
fine

cue0147019
00:44:10.280 --> 00:44:12.740
but

cue0147020
00:44:12.740 --> 00:44:13.580
the Betaddin

cue0147021
00:44:13.580 --> 00:44:15.000
the Supreme

cue0147022
00:44:15.000 --> 00:44:15.620
Court of Israel

cue0147023
00:44:15.620 --> 00:44:16.500
has

cue0147024
00:44:16.500 --> 00:44:18.180
three realms

cue0147025
00:44:18.180 --> 00:44:18.920
of authority

cue0147026
00:44:18.920 --> 00:44:20.120
three

cue0147027
00:44:20.120 --> 00:44:20.960
which are very

cue0147028
00:44:20.960 --> 00:44:21.420
important

cue0147029
00:44:21.420 --> 00:44:23.920
realm number

cue0147030
00:44:23.920 --> 00:44:24.320
one

cue0147031
00:44:24.320 --> 00:44:26.760
the transmission

cue0147032
00:44:26.760 --> 00:44:27.360
of those laws

cue0147033
00:44:27.360 --> 00:44:27.760
that we get

cue0147034
00:44:27.760 --> 00:44:28.520
from Moshe Misinai.

cue0147035
00:44:30.200 --> 00:44:31.520
And only the Bedina Gadol

cue0147036
00:44:31.520 --> 00:44:34.020
has the right

cue0147037
00:44:34.020 --> 00:44:36.240
to tell you, this we receive from Moshe Misinai.

cue0147038
00:44:39.120 --> 00:44:39.960
I'll give you an example.

cue0147039
00:44:40.060 --> 00:44:42.360
The laws of Terefot, the laws of Tefillin, the laws of Sukka.

cue0147040
00:44:43.300 --> 00:44:44.080
This was transmitted

cue0147041
00:44:44.080 --> 00:44:45.640
to us through Bedina Gadol

cue0147042
00:44:45.640 --> 00:44:47.960
and Bedina Gadol, which is the Supreme Court

cue0147043
00:44:47.960 --> 00:44:48.440
of Israel,

cue0147044
00:44:49.980 --> 00:44:51.220
had the authority

cue0147045
00:44:51.220 --> 00:44:53.980
to transmit the Tora from Moshe Misinai.

cue0147046
00:44:54.820 --> 00:44:56.000
Moshe Kibbel did not transmit the Tora from Misinai.

cue0147047
00:44:56.000 --> 00:44:58.900
Israel Yahshua, who was the head of the Jewish nation,

cue0147048
00:44:59.800 --> 00:45:01.620
Neḇiʾim la'zekenim,

cue0147049
00:45:01.700 --> 00:45:03.860
zekenim are the Jewish Sanhedrin,

cue0147050
00:45:04.420 --> 00:45:05.360
the Jewish Supreme Court.

cue0147051
00:45:05.860 --> 00:45:06.080
Fine.

cue0147052
00:45:06.540 --> 00:45:09.720
So we have one wrap.

cue0147053
00:45:10.860 --> 00:45:11.340
Second,

cue0147054
00:45:12.900 --> 00:45:14.460
they have the right

cue0147055
00:45:14.460 --> 00:45:16.500
to interpret the pasuq.

cue0147056
00:45:17.800 --> 00:45:18.460
And they own.

cue0147057
00:45:20.320 --> 00:45:21.580
Because no matter

cue0147058
00:45:21.580 --> 00:45:23.720
who you are,

cue0147059
00:45:23.720 --> 00:45:26.760
the world is constantly changing

cue0147060
00:45:26.760 --> 00:45:29.660
and it is up to

cue0147061
00:45:29.660 --> 00:45:30.920
the haqqamim

cue0147062
00:45:30.920 --> 00:45:33.740
to interpret

cue0147063
00:45:33.740 --> 00:45:36.520
this interpretation

cue0147064
00:45:36.520 --> 00:45:38.300
becomes law

cue0147065
00:45:38.300 --> 00:45:42.220
when it is done

cue0147066
00:45:42.220 --> 00:45:43.160
through the Yod Gimal

cue0147067
00:45:43.160 --> 00:45:44.340
there is a 13

cue0147068
00:45:44.340 --> 00:45:45.760
Yod Gimal Middosh

cue0147069
00:45:45.760 --> 00:45:46.820
but

cue0147070
00:45:46.820 --> 00:45:50.080
has to be submitted to a vote

cue0147071
00:45:50.080 --> 00:45:52.980
and the Sanhedrin

cue0147072
00:45:52.980 --> 00:45:54.260
has to agree upon it.

cue0147073
00:45:55.380 --> 00:45:55.920
And therefore,

cue0147074
00:45:56.340 --> 00:45:57.480
that's why I make it also

cue0147075
00:45:57.480 --> 00:45:58.900
in my Cardozo Law Review,

cue0147076
00:45:59.400 --> 00:46:01.740
I discuss very extensively this point,

cue0147077
00:46:02.260 --> 00:46:03.980
but then it is law,

cue0147078
00:46:04.580 --> 00:46:06.380
not by virtue of the exegesis

cue0147079
00:46:06.380 --> 00:46:07.620
of the interpretation,

cue0147080
00:46:08.180 --> 00:46:10.680
but by virtue of being passed

cue0147081
00:46:10.680 --> 00:46:11.500
by the Sanhedrin.

cue0147082
00:46:11.820 --> 00:46:12.080
In other words,

cue0147083
00:46:12.080 --> 00:46:13.600
you could be the greatest Darshan in the world.

cue0147084
00:46:14.460 --> 00:46:14.740
Alright?

cue0147085
00:46:15.780 --> 00:46:17.100
You could say the Darshan,

cue0147086
00:46:17.500 --> 00:46:17.960
and nobody,

cue0147087
00:46:18.360 --> 00:46:19.420
the Sanhedrin doesn't want to,

cue0147088
00:46:19.500 --> 00:46:20.580
does not agree with it.

cue0147089
00:46:22.980 --> 00:46:23.980
It's not a law.

cue0147090
00:46:24.620 --> 00:46:26.520
It becomes a law only

cue0147091
00:46:26.520 --> 00:46:30.400
if it is approved by the Sanhedrin.

cue0147092
00:46:31.420 --> 00:46:34.000
And because it depends on the Sanhedrin,

cue0147093
00:46:35.780 --> 00:46:37.380
tomorrow another Sanhedrin

cue0147094
00:46:37.380 --> 00:46:39.700
could say, we don't like this law.

cue0147095
00:46:41.420 --> 00:46:42.680
And they could abrogate it.

cue0147096
00:46:43.100 --> 00:46:44.280
Because that law

cue0147097
00:46:44.280 --> 00:46:46.320
came through legislation,

cue0147098
00:46:46.680 --> 00:46:48.080
not through tradition.

cue0147099
00:46:49.920 --> 00:46:50.220
You understand?

cue0147100
00:46:50.220 --> 00:46:53.060
I'm going to give you some examples

cue0147101
00:46:53.060 --> 00:46:54.440
I'll give you some examples

cue0147102
00:46:54.440 --> 00:46:55.460
in a minute

cue0147103
00:46:55.460 --> 00:46:58.880
and finally then there are laws which have nothing to do

cue0147104
00:46:58.880 --> 00:47:00.440
with the pasuq of the Tora

cue0147105
00:47:00.440 --> 00:47:03.520
they are takanot and gezerot

cue0147106
00:47:03.520 --> 00:47:04.220
sayagla Tora

cue0147107
00:47:04.220 --> 00:47:06.840
and that's the third

cue0147108
00:47:06.840 --> 00:47:08.820
realm of the Bet Din

cue0147109
00:47:08.820 --> 00:47:14.760
about buying and selling a shabbat

cue0147110
00:47:14.760 --> 00:47:16.160
it's not written in no place

cue0147111
00:47:16.160 --> 00:47:19.100
the homage never says

cue0147112
00:47:19.100 --> 00:47:25.280
If you look in the Gemaraʾ

cue0147113
